  "problem": "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx=2-{t}^{2},\\,y=t+1,\\,-1\\le t\\le 3\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=2-{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $-7$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=t+1.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $-7$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073429/assets/e06724560817f82e97c4606754a704cef47832ed89ab458dc3072622ce71d158.png)",
